{
 "name": "incident",
 "about": "The mainnet incident of 2026-11-08: a Deeploy operation that cannot finish. First some history is made (16 jobs deployed, 3 updated, 4 deleted), because the oracles re-read every past operation and the secret revisions on each pass. Then a job of production size is deployed on worker r1w-02, the worker disappears and the job is deleted: the operation stays open. What matters is how much chain-store traffic the open operation makes every oracle carry and whether ordinary chain-store users still get their writes confirmed. In the last phase one seed oracle also loses most of its CPU, as r1s-04 had on mainnet.",
